    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43599" root="&#xA;                        مسى&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسَآءٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>Afternoon, counted from noon to sunset:</i> (Az, IKoot, Mgh, Msb, TA:) or, accord.
to some, <i>to midnight:</i> (TA:) <i>contr. of</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبَاح</span>:
(S, K, Msb, &amp;c.:) and <i>evening, after sunset.</i>
(Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَيْتُهُ ذَا مَسَآءٍ</span> [<i>I came to him in the
evening</i>]. (IAar, TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صبح</span>.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبَاحٌ</span>.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَيْتُةُ صَبَاحًا مَسَآءً</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبَاحٌ</span>.

